s=f'<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 950 850"><title>Order-line star schema</title><desc>Unique dimension keys filter Sales through one-to-many relationships; Sales grain is one order line.</desc><rect width="100%" height="100%" fill="white"/><g font-family="sans-serif"><text x="30" y="45" font-size="28" fill="{N}">Star schema: one row per order line</text><defs><marker id="arr" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="10" refX="8" refY="3" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L0,6 L8,3z" fill="{N}"/></marker></defs>'
for x,y,w,h,title,body in [(330,300,290,220,'Sales','OrderID + LineID (grain)|OrderDate / ProductKey|CustomerKey / RegionKey|Quantity / NetRevenue / Profit'),(330,90,290,120,'DimDate','Date (unique)|Year / Month / Quarter'),(20,330,260,120,'DimProduct','ProductKey (unique)|Product / Category'),(670,330,260,120,'DimRegion','RegionKey (unique)|Region'),(330,610,290,120,'DimCustomer','CustomerKey (unique)|Segment')]:
 s+=f'<rect x="{x}" y="{y}" width="{w}" height="{h}" fill="#eef2f7" stroke="{N}"/><text x="{x+15}" y="{y+30}" font-size="22" fill="{N}">{title}</text>'
 for i,t in enumerate(body.split('|')):s+=f'<text x="{x+15}" y="{y+62+i*30}" font-size="16" fill="{N}">{html.escape(t)}</text>'
for a,b,lab in [((475,210),(475,300),'1 → *'),((280,390),(330,390),'1 → *'),((670,390),(620,390),'1 → *'),((475,610),(475,520),'1 → *')]:s+=f'<path d="M{a[0]},{a[1]} L{b[0]},{b[1]}" stroke="{N}" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#arr)"/><text x="{(a[0]+b[0])/2+8}" y="{(a[1]+b[1])/2-12}" font-size="17" fill="{N}">{lab}</text>'
s+=f'<text x="30" y="795" font-size="17" fill="{N}">Single-direction filtering: dimension → fact. OrderID can repeat across lines.</text></g></svg>';(O/'l22-star.svg').write_text(s);record('l22-star','Order-line star schema','Dimension keys are unique. Sales contains one order line; distinct orders differ from row count.','Four dimensions connect with one-to-many dimension-to-fact arrows to Sales.',[22],'Can OrderID be the unique key of this fact?','No; orders can have multiple lines. Use OrderID plus LineID.')
diagram('l23-context','Row context and filter context',[('Four lines, three orders','North: O1/L1=100, O1/L2=50. South: O2/L1=200, O3/L1=150 USD.'),('Row-level calculation','Quantity × UnitPrice × (1 − Discount) evaluates a value for each line.'),('No region filter','Total=500; Line Count=4; Order Count=3; AOV=500/3 USD.'),('North filter context','Total=150; Line Count=2; Order Count=1; AOV=150 USD.'),('Context transition','CALCULATE can convert row context into filter context; use keys to identify rows.')], 'Synthetic example. COUNTROWS measures lines; DISTINCTCOUNT(OrderID) measures orders.',[23],'What is AOV if you divide total by four lines?','125 USD is average line revenue, not average order value.')
diagram('l24-time-context','Date sets control time intelligence',[('Current selection','February 2024: February 1–29, within the complete 2022–2024 calendar.'),('Year to date','January 1–February 29, 2024; other dimension filters remain.'),('Prior-year period','February 2023 for a February-2024 comparison; document leap-day semantics.'),('Full-history cumulative','All calendar dates up to the selected cutoff; remove the whole DimDate context.'),('Selected-window cumulative','Only selected dates up to the cutoff; use ALLSELECTED and explain the window.')], 'Classic date-column patterns require a suitable calendar and relationship. A missing prior-year fact period may correctly return BLANK.',[24],'Why remove the whole date table for full-history totals?','A remaining Year/Month filter could constrain the cumulative date set.')
diagram('l25-performance','Measure performance; do not invent improvements',[('Baseline','Record Performance Analyzer duration for the same visual and filter state.'),('Reduce unnecessary storage','Remove unused columns; retain relationship keys. Hiding only affects usability.'),('Simplify model and measures','Check cardinality, single-direction relationships, unnecessary iterators, and Auto Date/Time.'),('Repeat controlled measurement','Use the same machine, query, refresh state, and repeated runs; separate cold/warm effects.'),('Report evidence','Compare durations and model size; a change may not improve speed.')], 'Procedure, not fabricated benchmark results. Native Power BI measurements must be supplied by executing Desktop.',[25],'Does hiding a column reduce model storage?','No; removing a stored column can.')
diagram('l26-project','Dashboard project acceptance criteria',[('Frame','Specify one decision, KPI formulas, grain, units and time scope.'),('Build','Load star tables, define measures, and test known reference totals.'),('Interact','Test year and region filters, reset, detail views, and no-data states.'),('Optimize','Measure performance; simplify only with verified correctness.'),('Submit','Model/report, data dictionary, QA notes, limitations, and screenshots.')], 'The bundled interactive HTML report demonstrates concepts; a Power BI submission still requires a .pbix built in Desktop.',[26],'What proves the dashboard total is correct?','Reconcile it to source/Python reference totals under identical filters.')
diagram('l27-ethics','Ethics at every project stage',[('Collection','Minimize fields, verify permission and coverage; avoid unnecessary identifiers.'),('Cleaning','Inspect group-dependent missingness; do not erase rare valid records.'),('Analysis','Report uncertainty and alternatives; avoid cherry-picking and causal overclaims.'),('Visualization and sharing','Use honest scales, accessible design, permissions and aggregation.'),('Pseudonymization is not anonymity','Hashed IDs may remain linkable; assess re-identification and retention.')], 'Risk review is continuous. Synthetic teaching data avoids exposing patient or customer identities.',[27],'Does hashing guarantee anonymous data?','No; linkage and re-identification can remain possible.')
diagram('l27-proposal','Capstone proposal canvas',[('Decision and scope','Stakeholder, problem, analytical questions, KPIs, units and denominator.'),('Data','Source, permission, grain, provenance, coverage, and quality risks.'),('Methods','Cleaning, EDA, model/report approach, validation, and alternatives.'),('Deliverables and milestones','Proposal → clean data/EDA → dashboard QA → presentation.'),('Acceptance and limitations','Reference checks, uncertainty, privacy, feasibility, and explicit exclusions.')], 'Proposal criteria are course guidance, not a claim of institutional assessment policy.',[27],'What makes a proposal feasible?','A bounded question, accessible data, realistic methods and explicit acceptance criteria.')
diagram('l28-checkpoints','Capstone lab checkpoints',[('Source and profile','Record grain, units, schema, permissions, and missingness.'),('Clean and validate','Keep raw data; log decisions and quarantine; check totals.'),('EDA','Inspect distributions, groups, and time; distinguish counts from rates.'),('Draft evidence','Link each insight to a chart and limitation.'),('Feedback loop','Failed checks return to their source stage; revise data/methods before dashboard build.')], 'A surprising finding is not mandatory: honest, reproducible evidence is more valuable than a dramatic narrative.',[28],'What if the EDA contradicts the proposal hypothesis?','Report it honestly and revise the interpretation.')
diagram('l29-qa','Final dashboard quality checks',[('Numbers','Match source/Python totals and distinct counts at the same grain.'),('Filters and dates','Test combinations, subtotals, date gaps, and legitimate no-data states.'),('Access and ethics','Test roles, remove unnecessary identifiers, expose limitations.'),('Performance and accessibility','Measure actual loads; test keyboard, contrast and labels.'),('Fix and retest','Trace a failure to data, measures or interactions; preserve a correction log.')], 'Example failures: multiplied join rows, order-line counts mislabeled as orders, stale refresh, or inaccessible color-only status.',[29],'How can a plausible number still be wrong?','Incorrect grain, joins or filter context can produce believable but invalid totals.')
diagram('l30-story','Presentation: evidence to decision',[('Question','Who needs to decide what, and why does the KPI matter?'),('Data and methods','Source, grain, cleaning, validation, and important assumptions.'),('Evidence','Show 2–3 clear findings, the filter context, and reproducible numbers.'),('Recommendation','State a proportionate next action and how it would be evaluated.'),('Limits and defence','Uncertainty, bias, unavailable denominators, and what cannot be claimed.')], 'Use associated with for observational findings. Reserve causal claims for appropriate designs and assumptions.',[30],'What belongs next to the recommendation?','Its evidence, limits, and an evaluation plan.')
